WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
OSHA 10 is not optional. You need this to work on most commercial job sites.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Hazard communication (HazCom) and the Globally Harmonized System (GHS). Safety
Data Sheets (SDS) have 16 standardized sections covering chemical
identification, hazards, first aid, fire-fighting, handling, exposure controls,

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
SDS: Safety Data Sheet. 16 sections covering chemical hazards, handling, and
emergency procedures.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
GHS Pictogram: Standardized symbols identifying chemical hazard types.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: You must know how to find and read an SDS
for any chemical you work with.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: 16 sections in every SDS. And — Know where SDS are kept on
your job site

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

